</tbody>
</table>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 1: </span>Average argument ranking performance of four LLMs on DebatePedia, using different instruction strategies. We report Spearman’s <math id="S5.T1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ρ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho</annotation></semantics></math> and Kendall’s <math id="S5.T1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math>. Bold marks the best-performing technique. All methods outperform the vanilla baseline, with CoT few-shot scoring the highest on average.</figcaption>
</figure>
