<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 4: </span>Argument ranking performance of various LLMs on the three acts of 12AngryMen, using different instruction strategies. We report Spearman’s <math id="S5.T4.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ρ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho</annotation></semantics></math> and Kendall’s <math id="S5.T4.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math>. Bold marks the best LLM per metric within each act. Although performance varies across models and acts, all instruction strategies improve results. Notably, every model does better on the smaller Act 3, suggesting challenges in larger, more complex debates.</figcaption>
</figure>
