<section id="A5" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix E </span>DeepSeek R1 vs. General-Purpose Models (Plots)</h2>

<figure id="A5.F11" class="ltx_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2">
<figure id="A5.F11.sf1" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2509.15739v1/12angrymen_DeepseekR1.svg" id="A5.F11.sf1.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_portrait" style="aspect-ratio:476/728;" width="476" height="728"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">(a) </span>Comparison on 12AngryMen dataset</figcaption>
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2">
<figure id="A5.F11.sf2" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2509.15739v1/debatepedia_DeepseekR1.svg" id="A5.F11.sf2.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_portrait" style="aspect-ratio:476/728;" width="476" height="728"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">(b) </span>Comparison on DebatePedia dataset</figcaption>
</figure></div></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 11: </span>Argument ranking performance of DeepSeek R1 vs. the average of four general-purpose models across instruction settings; bars show Spearman’s <math id="A5.F11.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ρ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho</annotation></semantics></math> and Kendall’s <math id="A5.F11.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math>. <span id="A5.F11.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">(a)</span> <span id="A5.F11.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">12AngryMen</span>: R1 is comparable to the average of general-purpose models and benefits from one and few-shot CoT. <span id="A5.F11.8" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">(b)</span> <span id="A5.F11.9" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">DebatePedia</span>: R1 underperforms all general-purpose models; CoT exemplars improve format adherence and recall but do not close the gap.</figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="A5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Figure <a href="#A5.F11" title="Figure 11 ‣ Appendix E DeepSeek R1 vs. General-Purpose Models (Plots) ‣ Can LLMs Judge Debates?Evaluating Non-Linear Reasoning via Argumentation Theory Semantics" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">11</span></a> compares <em id="A5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">DeepSeek R1</em> to the <em id="A5.p1.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">average</em> of our four general-purpose models across instruction setups on <span id="A5.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">12AngryMen</span> and <span id="A5.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">DebatePedia</span>, reporting Spearman <math id="A5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ρ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho</annotation></semantics></math> (top) and Kendall <math id="A5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math> (bottom).</p>
</div>
</section>
